					<span class="printuser avatarhover"><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drsevere" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(511038); return false;"  ><img class="small" src="http://www.wikidot.com/avatar.php?userid=511038&amp;amp;size=small&amp;amp;timestamp=1607267163" alt="DrSevere" style="background-image:url(http://www.wikidot.com/userkarma.php?u=511038)"/></a><a href="http://www.wikidot.com/user:info/drsevere" onclick="WIKIDOT.page.listeners.userInfo(511038); return false;" >DrSevere</a></span> <span class="odate time_1313585503 format_%25e%20%25b%20%25Y%2C%20%25H%3A%25M%7Cagohover">17 Aug 2011 12:51</span>
														</div>
			</div>
			<div class="content" id="post-content-1231882">
									

<p>As I read this, my thought process was as follows &quot;Mhmm&#8230;okay, solid&#8230;..oh wow, mobius strip, that's pretty cool&#8230;..oh man, this is getting really good, I can't wait to see what it actually does!&#8230;&#8230;wait, that's it?&quot;</p>
<p>In short, you have a great build up that lead me up to&#8230;not a whole lot. You had a really cool idea with the 5th track being basically hidden, but then when you actually get to what the hidden track actually <em>does</em>, it completely fizzles out. Plus:</p>
<p>6. Things what make you go nuts for no apparent reason.</p>
<p>Making you suicidal is just a more boring version of this item on the list.</p>
<p>So yeah, solid idea that starts off really well, then fizzles out to nothing. Downvoted for now, but if you can work on the ending (maybe talk to some people in chat for help if you are stumped), I can see this actually being a great SCP.</p>
<p>EDIT: Nice improvement. Still not as good as I think it could be, but good enough to deserve an upvote. Well done.</p>

							</div>

								
